---
title: Vegetable Stock
source: The Novelli Academy ("Beside the Seaside" Course, 20th April 2018)
author: Jean-Christophe Novelli
locale: en_GB
difficulty: Easy
prep time: 15m
cook time: 30m
diet: Vegetarian
tags:
- ingredient
- vegetarian
- savoury
---

Place all the vegetables (@celeriac{1}, @onions{3}, @potatoes{6%small}, and @carrots{3}) in a large pan and place over a high heat, shaking the pan occasionally.

> Other vegetables can be added or substituted: courgettes, turnips, parsnips, sweet potatoes, asparagus, etc.

Add all your @spices/herbs{} and cook for ~{2%minutes}.

> Spices and herbs to taste: fennel, caraway, thyme, bay leaves, star anise, coriander seeds, garlic cloves, cumin seeds, mustard seeds.

Add the @sugar{1%tbsp} and @salt{pinch} and immediately (otherwise the sugar will burn) add enough @water to cover the vegetables and bring to a fast boil; cook for ~{2%minutes}.

Reduce the heat and skim any impurity from the top of the stock. Boil for 20 to ~{25%minutes}.

Lift all the vegetable out of the pan and place in a large bowl. The stock is ready to use, or for a more concentrated flavour reduce over a low heat until the desired taste is reached.

> Season the vegetables with a sprinkle of sugar, your preferred herbs, a little sea salt and finally some olive oil, mix well. The vegetables can be used immediately as an accompaniment for other dishes or you can cool them down and use over the next few days by roasting them, sautéing them etc.